Summary: Hide the Metal performance HUD in launcher windows, but not in the games they start
Category: graphics
Kind: workaround
Origin: reconstructed
  Version: Sikarugir 10.0_8
  Binary: WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 ntdll.so
  Functions: the launcher check at 0x21900
  Changes: the value is kept in WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED and restored in
    processes that aren't launchers (10.0_8 drops it for the launcher's
    children too)
  Note: Sikarugir-only: no CrossOver 26, wine-staging or WineHQ equivalent
Upstream: no
Why: With MTL_HUD_ENABLED set, macOS draws the Metal performance HUD over every
 Metal window, launchers' included. When a launcher or overlay process is kept
 off a renderer DLL path (ntdll-renderer-dll-paths' list), ntdll removes
 MTL_HUD_ENABLED from its environment at start, unless SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD
 is set (to anything). This happens in init_paths, before the Windows
 environment is built, so the launcher's children don't get the variable either;
 it is kept as WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED, and a process that isn't a
 launcher puts it back in its own environment at start, so the games a launcher
 starts still get the HUD.
 It happens only when at least one of WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL, WINEDLLPATH_D9VK or
 WINEDLLPATH_DXVK has an entry, as in 10.0_8.
Programs: Battle.net, EA app, Epic, EOS overlay, GOG Galaxy, Rockstar
 launcher/Social Club, Steam web helper and overlay, Ubisoft Connect: the
 Metal performance HUD shows over their windows
Matches: exe Battle.net.exe, battlenet.overlay.runtime.exe,
 BlizzardBrowser.exe, BlizzardError.exe, EACefSubProcess.exe,
 EADesktop.exe, Link2EA.exe, EpicGamesLauncher.exe, EpicWebHelper.exe,
 EOSOverlayRenderer-Win32-Shipping.exe,
 EOSOverlayRenderer-Win64-Shipping.exe, GalaxyClient.exe, GalaxyClient
 Helper.exe, GOG Galaxy Notifications Renderer.exe, steamwebhelper.exe,
 gameoverlayui.exe, gameoverlayui64.exe, UbisoftConnect.exe,
 UplayWebCore.exe, UpcElevationService.exe; path Rockstar
 Games\Launcher\Launcher.exe, Rockstar Games\Social
 Club\SocialClubHelper.exe
Enable: see ntdll-renderer-dll-paths (WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL, WINEDLLPATH_D9VK or WINEDLLPATH_DXVK with an entry)
 env SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD=<anything> (turns it off: launchers keep the HUD)
Known issues: SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD is tested for presence only, so "0"
 also keeps the HUD. The game gets MTL_HUD_ENABLED back in its Unix
 environment, which Metal reads, but not in its Windows one
 (GetEnvironmentVariable), which comes from the launcher's.
Expects before it: ntdll-renderer-dll-paths
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: the value is restored for processes a launcher starts
 (the review's bug, measured on 10.0 build0)
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick builds 20261126T013940 and T024442 (macOS 26.7.2,
 M1 Max): smoke and the regression suite passed

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -423,10 +423,34 @@ static const struct
 
 static BOOL use_renderer_dll_path( unsigned int idx )
 {
-    if (renderer_dll_paths[idx].skip_for_launchers && is_launcher_process()) return FALSE;
+    if (renderer_dll_paths[idx].skip_for_launchers && is_launcher_process())
+    {
+        const char *hud;
+
+        /* launchers run without the Metal performance HUD unless asked to keep it;
+         * the value is kept for the games they start (restore_launcher_metal_hud) */
+        if (!getenv( "SIKARUGIR_KEEP_METAL_HUD" ) && (hud = getenv( "MTL_HUD_ENABLED" )))
+        {
+            setenv( "WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED", hud, 0 );
+            unsetenv( "MTL_HUD_ENABLED" );
+        }
+        return FALSE;
+    }
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* A process a launcher started gets back the MTL_HUD_ENABLED the launcher dropped.
+ * Its Unix environment comes from the launcher's Windows one, which has the value
+ * only as WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED. */
+static void restore_launcher_metal_hud(void)
+{
+    const char *hud = getenv( "WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED" );
+
+    if (!hud || getenv( "MTL_HUD_ENABLED" ) || is_launcher_process()) return;
+    setenv( "MTL_HUD_ENABLED", hud, 1 );
+    unsetenv( "WINE_LAUNCHER_MTL_HUD_ENABLED" );
+}
+
 static unsigned int count_path_list( const char *path )
 {
     unsigned int count = 1;
@@ -596,6 +620,7 @@ static void init_paths( char *argv[] )
     asprintf( &env, "WINELOADER=%s", wineloader );
     putenv( env );
 
+    restore_launcher_metal_hud();
     set_dll_path();
     set_system_dll_path();
     set_home_dir();
